{"data":{"actorId":"01KSK3QAE64QAADZ4Z86DY4771","createdAt":"2026-09-04T06:01:44.468Z","eventType":"comment.status_changed","id":"24","payload":{"from":"open","reason":"Fixed on the PR branch (e9d20fe8). CONFIRMED, and note the direction: this is NOT a leak but its inverse — provenance loss. The redactor tested for a leading '-' before considering whether a token was the pending value of an allowlisted option, so negative numbers were mistaken for unknown flags and dropped: ['run.py','--seed','\u003credacted\u003e','--max-questions','\u003credacted\u003e','--top-k','200']. Worth fixing precisely because the point of this block is that the artifact says what actually ran.\n\nThe finding's BROADER phrasing was deliberately NOT taken. It proposed consuming pending_safe_value before interpreting a leading '-' as an option; that reintroduces the leak this file has already been fixed for three times — '--top-k --mem0-api-key=sk-SECRET' would record the second token verbatim as --top-k's value. Implemented narrowly instead: a pending value is consumed only when the token matches argparse's own _negative_number_matcher (-\\d+$|-\\d*\\.\\d+$). argparse rejects that malformed command line anyway ('expected one argument'), so the narrow rule loses nothing real while keeping the guarantee, and the guard has its own test (test_a_negative_number_is_not_a_licence_to_consume_any_token). Verified '--seed -1 --max-questions -1 --rpm -2.5' all survive intact and '--debug -1' (a toggle with no pending value) still redacts conservatively.","to":"resolved"},"reviewId":"01M1NFRGNAA9V2A5YY9RESEQC7","targetId":"01M1NFRGNF7169JCJ0BAGA36VX","targetType":"review_comment","trailId":"01M1NC2KDB8G41TMVXFNRMSDX4"},"event":"comment.status_changed"}
{"data":{"actorId":null,"createdAt":"2026-09-04T06:01:58.294Z","eventType":"monitor.updated","id":"25","payload":{"boolean_value":null,"head_sha":"e9d20fe81a6a0a7068a8d52b5c08a052417b2721","label":"Risk","monitor_key":"risk","percent_value":24,"polarity":"lower_is_better","rationale":"Change is entirely within the bench/memory Python harness (argv redaction, FAIR_MODE knob list, secret fingerprinting) plus new tests/CI; it does not touch the Go provider's schema, symbol IDs, parser, streaming, CLI, no-egress, or CGO builds. Redaction uses a fail-closed allowlist and is test-covered, so worst-case impact is limited to benchmark-provenance artifacts, not the frozen wire contract or downstream Entire Brain.","run_id":"01M1NG3G1KF72ZF3BWSNBV32EM","runner_id":"trail-risk","size_value":null,"value_type":"percent"},"reviewId":null,"targetId":"risk","targetType":"trail_monitor","trailId":"01M1NC2KDB8G41TMVXFNRMSDX4"},"event":"monitor.updated"}
{"data":{"actorId":null,"createdAt":"2026-09-04T06:02:08.565Z","eventType":"monitor.updated","id":"26","payload":{"boolean_value":null,"head_sha":"e9d20fe81a6a0a7068a8d52b5c08a052417b2721","label":"Security","monitor_key":"security","percent_value":6,"polarity":"lower_is_better","rationale":"Changes are confined to the memory benchmark harness and are net security-improving: argv/URL credential redaction and secret-name fingerprinting close an artifact-leak, and the new CI job uses read-only permissions, no persisted credentials, and pinned actions. No egress, runtime downloads, dependency changes, or unsafe subprocess/path handling are introduced; the only exec() runs a bounded in-repo patch artifact under test.","run_id":"01M1NG3G1Y39Y4QG41A781SW29","runner_id":"trail-security","size_value":null,"value_type":"percent"},"reviewId":null,"targetId":"security","targetType":"trail_monitor","trailId":"01M1NC2KDB8G41TMVXFNRMSDX4"},"event":"monitor.updated"}
