{"data":{"actorId":null,"createdAt":"2026-09-04T06:08:03.890Z","eventType":"code_version.created","id":"29","payload":{"baseSha":null,"headSha":"0abeba3eeb8401aedbc5901f20c2b3f4d07f2223"},"reviewId":null,"targetId":"01M1NGG29P0T5GXEYPQA79N7C4","targetType":"code_version","trailId":"01M1NC2KDB8G41…17267 tokens truncated…The remedy is BOUNDED, deliberately. 'hash untracked file contents' unqualified is pathological here: the real entire-graph checkout carries 41 untracked non-ignored files totalling 78,487,812 bytes, 78,235,456 of which is one untracked build artifact (entire-graph-linux-amd64), and capture() runs at four metadata sites per run. So: hash smallest-first under a 32 MiB / 512 file budget, and record anything past the budget as `over-budget size:N` rather than dropping it, keeping the digest a total function of the untracked set. Measured on that live dirty checkout: cold 0.044s, warm 0.031s, 40 of 41 files content-hashed, one over-budget entry 'entire-graph-linux-amd64 -\u003e over-budget size:78235456', digest stable across calls.\n\nPROOF (compile-clean revert). Restoring only the one behavioural line\n  state[\"dirty_digest\"] = _fingerprint(status + \"\\n\" + _run(\"git\", \"diff\", \"HEAD\"))\nleaving _untracked_digest_lines() defined (ast.parse: 'compiles clean'), then\n  python3 -B -m unittest bench.memory.benchmarks.common.test_runmeta\nfails 2 of 65:\n\nFAIL: test_untracked_file_contents_reach_the_dirty_digest\n  AssertionError: 'sha256:fd371ee20fa0' == 'sha256:fd371ee20fa0' : two untracked implementations serialize to one provenance\n\nFAIL: test_untracked_content_hashing_is_budgeted\n  self.assertNotEqual(base[\"dirty_digest\"], resized[\"dirty_digest\"])\n  AssertionError: 'sha256:2cdf5f6d9c97' == 'sha256:2cdf5f6d9c97'\n\nWith the fix restored: Ran 65 tests, OK; and the full CI guard set (test_runmeta + ci.test_locomo_search_retry_patch) Ran 76 tests, OK, after merging origin/main (go build ./... clean).","to":"resolved"},"reviewId":"01M1P7AD