{"data":{"actorId":"01KSK3QAE64QAADZ4Z86DY4771","createdAt":"2026-09-05T16:21:59.839Z","eventType":"comment.status_changed","id":"146","payload":{"from":"open","reason":"CONFIRMED -- a real regression I introduced in a7261b8c, reproduced as a permanent hang, fixed in aaa2d131.\n\nReproduced first. A temp repo with one untracked symlink to /dev/zero:\n  git ls-files --others --exclude-standard  -\u003e  'zero_link'\n  os.stat('zero_link').st_size = 0   (S_ISCHR: True)\n  git_state(root) did not return within 10s\nos.stat follows the link, the device reports size 0, so it passes any byte budget, and _file_digest then loops on 'fh.read(1 \u003c\u003c 20)' which never returns b''. Metadata capture reads forever. The premise is exactly right and a byte budget is no defence against it.\n\nFix (bench/memory/benchmarks/common/runmeta.py, _untracked_digest_lines):\n  entry  = os.lstat(path)                       # never follows\n  linked = stat.S_ISLNK(entry.st_mode)\n  target = os.stat(path) if linked else entry\n  if not stat.S_ISREG(target.st_mode):\n      lines.append(f\"{name}\\0{label}not-a-regular-file mode:{target.st_mode:#o}\")\n      continue\nNothing that is not a regular file is ever opened. Devices, FIFOs, sockets and directories are recorded by mode; a dangling link or symlink loop raises OSError from lstat/stat and is recorded 'unreadable'.\n\nOne deviation from the prescribed remedy, deliberate: it said to reject symlinks outright. Symlinks are followed, but only to a regular file. An untracked implementation file may legitimately be a symlink and its target is what actually ran, so rejecting the class would lose exactly the provenance this digest exists to bind. The entry is labelled 'symlink ' so replacing a file with a link to identical bytes still moves the digest -- the substitution that a blanket reject would have made invisible. Documented residual, in place: a regular file swapped for a device between the stat and the open would still be read; closing that needs O_NONBLOCK plus an fstat, which no non-adversarial checkout needs.\n\nPROOF (compile-clean revert). Restoring only the previous os.stat-without-a-mode-check loop body, keeping 'import stat' so nothing breaks at import (ast.parse: 'compiles clean'), then\n  python3 -B -m unittest bench.memory.benchmarks.common.test_runmeta\nfails 2 of 67, and the suite's wall clock goes from 1.4s to 16.6s:\n\nFAIL: test_an_untracked_device_symlink_is_never_read\n  self.assertLess(elapsed, 5.0, ...)\n  AssertionError: 15.001509250025265 not less than 5.0 : git_state spent 15.0s reading a character device\n  (15s is the test's SIGALRM watchdog firing inside the read; without a watchdog the call never returns at all. _file_digest catches OSError and TimeoutError is one, so on the reverted body the entry comes back as 'zero_link\\x00unreadable: TimeoutError' -- the read happened.)\n\nFAIL: test_a_symlinked_untracked_file_is_followed_and_labelled\n  AssertionError: 'sha256:72f20db519da' == 'sha256:72f20db519da' : a file swapped for a link to identical bytes\n\nWith the fix in place: 'Ran 67 tests ... OK', and the full CI guard set (test_runmeta + ci.test_locomo_search_retry_patch) 'Ran 78 tests ... OK'.","to":"resolved"},"reviewId":"01M1S5JC05W18V7E4HTPHV58N8","targetId":"01M1S5JC1GRC1571K88JMN6SN5","targetType":"review_comment","trailId":"01M1NC2KDB8G41TMVXFNRMSDX4"},"event":"comment.status_changed"}
