{"data":{"actorId":"01KSK3QAE64QAADZ4Z86DY4771","createdAt":"2026-09-04T06:22:29.274Z","eventType":"comment.status_changed","id":"46","payload":{"from":"open","reason":"Fixed on the PR branch (f5068b5f). CONFIRMED: ENTIRE_GRAPH_BIN / CMM_BIN / GRAPHIFY_SOURCE sat in SYMMETRIC_ARM_SETTINGS, but they select which BUILD implements an arm, and code_hashes() binds the harness rather than what it drives.\n\nThe finding's FIRST remedy was deliberately not taken, and the reasoning is the important part: rejecting the overrides closes nothing, because run_locomo.sh does not set them — it puts $HOME/bin on PATH — so the DEFAULT route is exactly as unbound as the override. Rejecting overrides would have produced the appearance of a fix while leaving the actual hole open.\n\nImplemented instead: implementation_provenance() records, for every arm implementation resolved from EITHER source, its path, whether it came from env or PATH, and its sha256, plus git commit and dirty state for GRAPHIFY_SOURCE. Digests are cached (capture runs at four sites) and an unreadable path is recorded rather than raised, so provenance capture cannot itself fail a run. Fail-without-fix: 4 errors + 1 failure, including KeyError 'ENTIRE_GRAPH_BIN' and \"'implementations' not found\".\n\nThis is complementary to the cmm binary verification on PR #204 (CMM_BIN required, no PATH fallback, patched-build fingerprint checked without executing): that one refuses an unverified binary for the one arm whose published row is patched, this one records what actually ran for every arm.","to":"resolved"},"reviewId":"01M1NGHWQDDT1XMQ6FN15GS9K0","targetId":"01M1NGHWQR6Z9D81CVZH7N0TX2","targetType":"review_comment","trailId":"01M1NC2KDB8G41TMVXFNRMSDX4"},"event":"comment.status_changed"}
