{"data":{"actorId":null,"createdAt":"2026-09-04T06:33:11.418Z","eventType":"monitor.updated","id":"58","payload":{"boolean_value":null,"head_sha":"a8eb42cf662f59f7bfd93776613662a28f2145b1","label":"Risk","monitor_key":"risk","percent_value":20,"polarity":"lower_is_better","rationale":"Change is fully contained to the vendored bench/memory Python kit (runmeta provenance/redaction, FAIR_MODE guards, a search-retry patch) plus a new CI job, with no touch to the Go provider, wire contract, stable IDs, parsers, streaming, public CLI, or CGO builds; the only trust-boundary aspect (secret redaction in committed artifacts) is what it strengthens and is backed by extensive new tests.","run_id":"01M1NHWBWRC0E7MDGVZPT1WYZW","runner_id":"trail-risk","size_value":null,"value_type":"percent"},"reviewId":null,"targetId":"risk","targetType":"trail_monitor","trailId":"01M1NC2KDB8G41TMVXFNRMSDX4"},"event":"monitor.updated"}
{"data":{"actorId":null,"createdAt":"2026-09-04T06:33:16.563Z","eventType":"monitor.updated","id":"59","payload":{"boolean_value":null,"head_sha":"a8eb42cf662f59f7bfd93776613662a28f2145b1","label":"Security","monitor_key":"security","percent_value":8,"polarity":"lower_is_better","rationale":"Changes are confined to the vendored bench/memory kit and are defensive hardening: argv/credential redaction and secret-env fingerprinting before persistence, URL scrubbing to scheme+fingerprinted-host, binary-digest provenance via local reads, plus a least-privilege CI job (contents:read, persist-credentials:false). No new egress, runtime downloads, dependency changes, or unsafe subprocess/path handling; the sole exec() runs trusted in-repo patch text under test.","run_id":"01M1NHWBX4AHHMYA4MX9MYJ3M8","runner_id":"trail-security","size_value":null,"value_type":"percent"},"reviewId":null,"targetId":"security","targetType":"trail_monitor","trailId":"01M1NC2KDB8G41TMVXFNRMSDX4"},"event":"monitor.updated"}
{"data":{"actorId":"01KSK3QAE64QAADZ4Z86DY4771","createdAt":"2026-09-04T06:33:26.430Z","eventType":"comment.status_changed","id":"60","payload":{"from":"open","reason":"Fixed on the PR branch (a8eb42cf). CONFIRMED — and it lands squarely on the exception the previous round explicitly argued for. The spec listed 'a host' as a valid derived form, but that contradicts the totality invariant the whole change exists to establish: a hostname can itself carry a tenant id or token, e.g. 'https://\u003ctenant\u003e.service.example/' was recorded verbatim. The authority is now sha256-fingerprinted — 'https://\u003credacted\u003e@sha256:c3a8d5514aef/\u003credacted\u003e?\u003credacted\u003e' — so the same host still fingerprints alike and remains comparable between runs, while the readable host stays available as env.MEM0_HOST. The test's _URL_LOCATION_RE is now genuinely closed, with no character class for a hostname. Fail-without-fix: reverting to verbatim fails with 'localhost unexpectedly found in http://localhost:18888' plus 8 witness failures.","to":"resolved"},"reviewId":"01M1NH7Q5GN194QP5ZW9CZXM3H","targetId":"01M1NH7Q5RG66NZKRGQFWXD8ZN","targetType":"review_comment","trailId":"01M1NC2KDB8G41TMVXFNRMSDX4"},"event":"comment.status_changed"}
{"data":{"actorId":"01KSK3QAE64QAADZ4Z86DY4771","createdAt":"2026-09-04T06:33:27.831Z","eventType":"comment.status_changed","id":"61","payload":{"from":"open","reason":"Fixed on the PR branch (a8eb42cf). CONFIRMED, and the most serious of the three because it undermines the one argv value deliberately kept verbatim for the downstream reader. patch 0003 line 197 does 'backend = os.getenv(\"MEM0_BACKEND\", args.backend)', so with FAIR_MODE=1, MEM0_BACKEND=oss and --backend entire there was NO SystemExit: the artifact could name 'entire' in argv while mem0 actually ran — a silently mislabelled arm, which is this project's worst failure class. MEM0_BACKEND is arm SELECTION, neither an asymmetry knob nor infrastructure, so it moved out of SYMMETRIC_ARM_SETTINGS into a new ARM_SELECTION_SETTINGS and must now equal the flag. An override that AGREES still passes, and no launcher sets it. Fail-without-fix: 'SystemExit not raised'.","to":"resolved"},"reviewId":"01M1NHBVMBF8ZAJ54NJRVFHMF2","targetId":"01M1NHBVMGGC2VGG3FVY4HRM3Z","targetType":"review_comment","trailId":"01M1NC2KDB8G41TMVXFNRMSDX4"},"event":"comment.status_changed"}
{"data":{"actorId":"01KSK3QAE64QAADZ4Z86DY4771","createdAt":"2026-09-04T06:33:29.155Z","eventType":"comment.status_changed","id":"62","payload":{"from":"open","reason":"Fixed on the PR branch (a8eb42cf). CONFIRMED — provenance loss, not a leak. entire_client.py:115 execs a bare name via PATH, so ENTIRE_GRAPH_BIN=entire-graph ran a real binary while provenance recorded 'unreadable: FileNotFoundError'. Now resolved with shutil.which when there is no path separator, recording resolved_via: literal|PATH. The agent also closed the adjacent gap this finding implies: an arm that sets NO override still runs a specific build, so CMM_BIN and GRAPHIFY_PYTHON fall back to the client module's own _DEFAULT_* values — read from sys.modules only if the run already imported the module, so there is no import side effect and no duplicated literal that could drift (the hazard the enum-sync test exists to catch). Fail-without-fix: \"'unreadable: FileNotFoundError' != 'sha256:75d6e376e79a...'\".","to":"resolved"},"reviewId":"01M1NHBVMBF8ZAJ54NJRVFHMF2","targetId":"01M1NHBVMKP9088TY2H4BCW6XZ","targetType":"review_comment","trailId":"01M1NC2KDB8G41TMVXFNRMSDX4"},"event":"comment.status_changed"}
