{"data":{"actorId":null,"createdAt":"2026-09-05T16:22:06.385Z","eventType":"monitor.updated","id":"148","payload":{"boolean_value":null,"head_sha":"aaa2d1312658aa9c635d87139cd864845c85bf55","label":"Security","monitor_key":"security","percent_value":8,"polarity":"lower_is_better","rationale":"All changes are defensive hardening of a benchmark provenance artifact: allowlist-based argv/env secret redaction (fixing a previously inverted filter that leaked credential-carrying vars), bounded in-repo untracked-file digesting with safe symlink/device handling, and a locked-down CI job (contents:read, persist-credentials:false, pinned actions, stdlib-only). Every subprocess call is argv-vector with no shell/eval, and there is no new network, dependency, or runtime-download path.","run_id":"01M1S5Z4VMA4KPFTN6FHN61S7Q","runner_id":"trail-security","size_value":null,"value_type":"percent"},"reviewId":null,"targetId":"security","targetType":"trail_monitor","trailId":"01M1NC2KDB8G41TMVXFNRMSDX4"},"event":"monitor.updated"}
{"data":{"actorId":"01KSK3QAE64QAADZ4Z86DY4771","createdAt":"2026-09-05T16:24:00.445Z","eventType":"comment.status_changed","id":"149","payload":{"from":"open","reason":"PREMISE CONFIRMED, remedy UNDERDETERMINED -- filed as https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/issues/217 rather than guessed at.\n\nReproduced. git_state() on a plain (non-git) directory:\n  A: {'commit': '', 'dirty': False}\n  B: {'commit': '', 'dirty': False}      # after rewriting impl.py in place\n  IDENTICAL: True\n  provenance entry: {'path': 'sha256:ed862663f2b2', 'source': 'env', 'commit': '', 'dirty': False}\nSo yes: two different source trees at one path produce byte-identical provenance for GRAPHIFY_SOURCE. Not disputed.\n\nBoth prescribed remedies were tested, and both break something:\n\n1. 'fail closed' aborts the kit's actual deployment shape. The bench kit is copied to VMs as a plain tree, not cloned. Copying bench/memory outside any checkout and calling capture() succeeds today -- 'git rev-parse --show-toplevel' -\u003e 'fatal: not a git repository', git block {'commit': '', 'dirty': False}, and 8 code_md5 entries still binding the harness. Failing closed turns every VM run into an abort, which is a policy change to when the harness refuses to run.\n\n2. 'hash the source tree' is unbounded. Without git there is no --exclude-standard, so nothing excludes __pycache__, .venv, build output or vendored data from an arbitrary checkout. This PR has already had to give the untracked digest an explicit 32 MiB / 512 file budget (a real tree carried a single 78 MB untracked artifact) and a regular-file guard (a symlink to /dev/zero hung capture forever, finding 01M1S5JC1GRC...). A source-tree hash inherits both and additionally needs an answer to 'which files are the implementation' -- an include list nobody has chosen.\n\nWorth recording, because it bounds the exposure: this gap is the ARM SOURCE CHECKOUT only. The harness itself is already content-bound without git -- code_hashes() md5s 8 files including runmeta.py and requirements-lock-py312.txt -- and does so precisely because the kit ships as a copied tree.\n\nDismissing rather than fixing is also a stop-condition call. runmeta.py provenance has now been flagged on three consecutive heads of this PR (dirty digest -\u003e device symlink -\u003e non-git source dir), each new finding raised against the previous fix. That is the thrash signal, and this remedy is a design decision, so it goes to #217 for the fairness-kit owner instead of a fourth speculative push.","to":"dismissed"},"reviewId":"01M1S60QTN4Q8YEJNJE0WNT3CF","targetId":"01M1S60QV9ER44KPYDRHR1XV5B","targetType":"review_comment","trailId":"01M1NC2KDB8G41TMVXFNRMSDX4"},"event":"comment.status_changed"}
