{"data":{"actorId":"01KSK3QAE64QAADZ4Z86DY4771","createdAt":"2026-09-04T06:08:42.384Z","eventType":"comment.status_changed","id":"31","payload":{"from":"open","reason":"Fixed on the PR branch (0abeba3e). CONFIRMED: the URL scrubber bailed out on any value without a network location and treated it as a plain non-URL, so 'file:///hooks/\u003csecret\u003e' and 'mailto:admin:\u003csecret\u003e@x' passed through verbatim. Fix: a scheme-bearing value with no authority keeps only its scheme ('file:\u003credacted\u003e') — there is no location worth preserving, and guessing which segment of an opaque URI is the secret is exactly the pattern-matching this filter exists to avoid.\n\nThe finding's LITERAL remedy was not taken, for the same reason as the previous round: 'redact scheme-bearing values without a network location' would also redact 'C:\\results\\locomo', because urlsplit reads 'C:' as a scheme — so a Windows --output-dir would silently become \u003credacted\u003e, destroying provenance exactly as the negative-number bug did. Single-letter schemes are therefore treated as drive letters, not URI schemes; real schemes here are always longer. Both directions verified: C:\\results\\locomo and c:/results/locomo survive intact, /results/locomo and gpt-5.6-sol untouched, http://localhost:18888 unchanged. Fail-without-fix: 3 failures including the property test finding the synthetic key inside '--mem0-host file:///hooks/...'.","to":"resolved"},"reviewId":"01M1NG5Z8FE4F1W8C29425Q46Y","targetId":"01M1NG5Z8QNW50BB1RH8BGRZFA","targetType":"review_comment","trailId":"01M1NC2KDB8G41TMVXFNRMSDX4"},"event":"comment.status_changed"}
