{"data":{"actorId":"01KSK3QAE64QAADZ4Z86DY4771","createdAt":"2026-09-04T07:00:18.479Z","eventType":"comment.status_changed","id":"88","payload":{"from":"open","reason":"Fixed on the PR branch (46f5fabd). CONFIRMED, and it OVERTURNS a trade-off defended in a code comment two rounds earlier. The prior argument was that a zero-context question is a defect signature and never a normal result; the finding is right that this corrupts the denominator from the other direction — a valid zero-match query was retried for ~35s and then counted as a drop. It also named the correct fix: an explicit failure signal.\n\nThat signal already existed. README section 3.2 documents making search() raise for every adapter that returned a silent []; mem0's client was the one missed. So patch 0002 now makes _search_oss and _search_cloud raise SEARCH_EXHAUSTED, and patch 0003 drops the heuristic entirely (_swallows_search_failure deleted). [] now means zero-match, and an exhausted search raises and is not retried again since the client already spent five attempts. The fix moved to the right layer and the wrapper got simpler.\n\nBoth patches regenerated against the pinned upstream: git apply --check clean, result parses, and the PRE-EDIT reconstruction reproduced the documented md5s exactly (44e36784... -\u003e 041f93a1...) before anything changed, which is what validates the new digests bb763cab... and ff548086.... Fail-without-fix: '0 != 2 : _search_oss and _search_cloud must both stop returning [] on exhaustion'.","to":"resolved"},"reviewId":"01M1NJC5G7J6YQHK3Z12PCXRS8","targetId":"01M1NJC5GC2KQ5NMRDKP66XATA","targetType":"review_comment","trailId":"01M1NC2KDB8G41TMVXFNRMSDX4"},"event":"comment.status_changed"}
{"data":{"actorId":"01KSK3QAE64QAADZ4Z86DY4771","createdAt":"2026-09-04T07:00:19.991Z","eventType":"comment.status_changed","id":"89","payload":{"from":"open","reason":"Fixed on the PR branch (46f5fabd). CONFIRMED — a regression introduced by this branch's own earlier work. asymmetry_report() treated any non-empty string as active, so the CORRECT way to disable a feature aborted the run: FAIR_MODE=1 with EG_DEEP=0 or MEM0_DATE_INJECT=false both aborted. Declared boolean and numeric knobs are now read before being called active. Unrecognised knobs still fail closed at 0 — with no declared domain there is no way to know that 0 means off — pinned by test_an_unrecognised_knob_still_fails_closed_when_zero.","to":"resolved"},"reviewId":"01M1NJQGYGBRMSZ8ZR3N546G9W","targetId":"01M1NJQGYN827A147NYEZJ2RY1","targetType":"review_comment","trailId":"01M1NC2KDB8G41TMVXFNRMSDX4"},"event":"comment.status_changed"}
{"data":{"actorId":"01KSK3QAE64QAADZ4Z86DY4771","createdAt":"2026-09-04T07:00:21.435Z","eventType":"comment.status_changed","id":"90","payload":{"from":"open","reason":"Fixed on the PR branch (46f5fabd). CONFIRMED: the MEM0_BACKEND mismatch went into the FAIR_MODE exception text raw, bypassing _env_value — which is exactly the two-call-sites-drifting failure the agent had written a comment about, in code it added the same round. Now routed through _env_value, so a free-form value fingerprints (MEM0_BACKEND=sha256:73c6af1cef38) while a valid arm name stays readable. Fail-without-fix: the synthetic key found in 'FAIR_MODE=1 but ... MEM0_BACKEND=https://sk-FAKETESTKEY-....host/'.","to":"resolved"},"reviewId":"01M1NJQGYGBRMSZ8ZR3N546G9W","targetId":"01M1NJQGYTNY5MY12FYQ2H348E","targetType":"review_comment","trailId":"01M1NC2KDB8G41TMVXFNRMSDX4"},"event":"comment.status_changed"}
{"data":{"actorId":"01KSK3QAE64QAADZ4Z86DY4771","createdAt":"2026-09-04T07:00:22.852Z","eventType":"comment.status_changed","id":"91","payload":{"from":"open","reason":"Fixed on the PR branch (46f5fabd). CONFIRMED: the implementations block published resolved paths verbatim while env_snapshot() fingerprints those same variables — the same value protected in one block and disclosed in another. Paths now fingerprint there too; the CONTENT digest is what identifies the build, so nothing needed for provenance is lost. Fail-without-fix: the synthetic key found in \"{'path': '/home/sk-FAKETESTKEY-.../bin/entire-graph', ...}\".","to":"resolved"},"reviewId":"01M1NJQGYGBRMSZ8ZR3N546G9W","targetId":"01M1NJQGYXT6RTZ630T81R2664","targetType":"review_comment","trailId":"01M1NC2KDB8G41TMVXFNRMSDX4"},"event":"comment.status_changed"}
