{"data":{"actorId":"01KSK3QAE64QAADZ4Z86DY4771","createdAt":"2026-09-04T07:37:56.598Z","eventType":"comment.status_changed","id":"116","payload":{"from":"open","reason":"Fixed on the PR branch (290c0d02). CONFIRMED, and it is the INVERSE defect created by this branch's own fix two rounds earlier. That round corrected EG_DEEP=0 wrongly aborting; the correction gave _is_active the wrong polarity for every DEFAULT-ON knob, so the fairness guard silently ALLOWED real arm changes: BM25_STEM=0 (disables stemming, client default 1), BM25_K1=0 (default 1.2) and CMM_MEM_BUDGET_MB=0 (default 4096) all passed FAIR_MODE. BM25_STOREDACTEDORDS=0 aborted only by accident, having no declared domain and so falling through to 'active if non-empty'.\n\nRoot cause named correctly: 'is this truthy' has no answer without the default — patching the symptom produced the opposite bug. Fixed by asking the right question instead: a knob is active when it DEVIATES FROM WHAT THE ARM DOES UNSET, with ENV_KNOB_DEFAULTS taken from each client's own os.getenv call and a coverage test that re-derives them from source and fails on drift. Both directions now come out right, plus a genuine bonus — EG_INGEST_GRANULARITY=session no longer aborts, and that is the PUBLISHED config.\n\nThree earlier tests were CORRECTED rather than accommodated: they asserted BM25_B=0.75, EG_INGEST_GRANULARITY=session and BM25_STEM=False were deviations. The first two are the clients' own defaults; the third is ambiguous and correctly aborts. Those tests encoded the wrong model. Fail-without-fix: 'SystemExit not raised' across 6 knobs.","to":"resolved"},"reviewId":"01M1NMT4120JC470A8MZVKFD49","targetId":"01M1NMT418FG6J0XBRXG42P3DE","targetType":"review_comment","trailId":"01M1NC2KDB8G41TMVXFNRMSDX4"},"event":"comment.status_changed"}
