{"data":{"actorId":"01KSK3QAE64QAADZ4Z86DY4771","createdAt":"2026-09-05T16:21:37.084Z","eventType":"comment.status_changed","id":"143","payload":{"from":"open","reason":"WRONG REMEDY (ran it), plus one false premise. Underdetermined residual filed as https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/issues/216.\n\n1. 'silently' is false. The branch is not silent: it logs\n     logger.error(\"SEARCH_DROP user=%s after %d attempts: %s\", user_id, _RETRY_MAX, str(last)[:200])\n   and the caller records \"search_dropped\": search_dropped in the per-question artifact, with an in-code note that any run carrying search_dropped=True questions must drop them symmetrically across arms or be re-run. A misconfiguration is therefore surfaced as an ERROR line per question and a drop count, not swallowed.\n\n2. The prescribed remedy inverts the patch. _is_retryable classifies by exception name/text; RuntimeError('SEARCH_EXHAUSTED after 5 attempts for user=u') and RuntimeError('BUFFER_MISSING for conversation 3') match none of the transient patterns and fall through to 'return False'. Those two strings ARE the documented per-question drop signals this patch exists to account for (patch 0002 SEARCH_EXHAUSTED; README 3.2 BUFFER_MISSING). Re-raising when _is_retryable is false therefore aborts the whole run on the exact signal the wrapper was written to count.\n\n   Not asserted -- executed. Applied the remedy verbatim to the patch text:\n     -            if not _is_retryable(exc) or attempt == _RETRY_MAX - 1:\n     -                break\n     +            if not _is_retryable(exc):\n     +                raise\n     +            if attempt == _RETRY_MAX - 1:\n     +                break\n   then:\n     python3 -B -m unittest bench.memory.ci.test_locomo_search_retry_patch\n   went from 'Ran 11 tests ... OK' to 'Ran 11 tests ... FAILED (errors=4)':\n     ERROR: test_an_exhausted_search_is_counted_as_a_drop\n     ERROR: test_an_exhausted_search_is_not_retried_again\n     ERROR: test_every_client_signals_failure_the_same_way (error='SEARCH_EXHAUSTED')\n     ERROR: test_every_client_signals_failure_the_same_way (error='BUFFER_MISSING')\n   each with 'RuntimeError: SEARCH_EXHAUSTED after 5 attempts for user=u' / 'RuntimeError: BUFFER_MISSING for conversation 3' escaping _search_with_retry. The patch was restored; the suite is back to 'Ran 11 tests ... OK'.\n\n3. What IS real and is NOT mine to decide: _is_retryable returns False for two unlike classes -- per-question drop signals (must be accounted) and global misconfiguration (authentication/permission/badrequest/notfound, which arguably should abort). Separating them is a harness fail-fast policy call, so it is filed as issue #216 rather than guessed at here. Exposure meanwhile is bounded: a broken credential drops every search, giving a ~100% drop rate in the artifact rather than a quietly wrong score.","to":"dismissed"},"reviewId":"01M1S5JC05W18V7E4HTPHV58N8","targetId":"01M1S5JC0TJA2A2A792WDABJJA","targetType":"review_comment","trailId":"01M1NC2KDB8G41TMVXFNRMSDX4"},"event":"comment.status_changed"}
