{"data":{"actorId":"01KSK3QAE64QAADZ4Z86DY4771","createdAt":"2026-09-05T16:13:11.534Z","eventType":"comment.status_changed","id":"135","payload":{"from":"open","reason":"CONFIRMED and fixed in 3a72e836 (behavioural change a7261b8c).\n\nReproduced first. git_state() built dirty_digest from `git status --porcelain` + `git diff HEAD`. `git diff HEAD` is tracked-only; porcelain gives untracked files as `?? name` with no content. A temp repo with one untracked file whose body changed from 'VARIANT ONE' to 'VARIANT TWO -- totally different':\n  status  = '?? untracked_impl.py\\n'\n  diff HEAD = ''\n  digest before = sha256:fd371ee20fa0\n  digest after  = sha256:fd371ee20fa0   (identical)\nSo the premise holds exactly as stated: two checkouts differing only in an untracked file's contents got one provenance stamp. This is reachable through implementation_provenance(), which calls git_state(GRAPHIFY_SOURCE).\n\nFix: _untracked_digest_lines() enumerates with `git ls-files --others --exclude-standard --full-name -z -- :/` (same set porcelain reports, so ignored output never enters), content-hashes each via the existing identity-cached _file_digest(), and folds `name\\0digest` lines into dirty_digest. With no untracked files the digest input is byte-identical to before.\n\nThe remedy is BOUNDED, deliberately. 'hash untracked file contents' unqualified is pathological here: the real entire-graph checkout carries 41 untracked non-ignored files totalling 78,487,812 bytes, 78,235,456 of which is one untracked build artifact (entire-graph-linux-amd64), and capture() runs at four metadata sites per run. So: hash smallest-first under a 32 MiB / 512 file budget, and record anything past the budget as `over-budget size:N` rather than dropping it, keeping the digest a total function of the untracked set. Measured on that live dirty checkout: cold 0.044s, warm 0.031s, 40 of 41 files content-hashed, one over-budget entry 'entire-graph-linux-amd64 -\u003e over-budget size:78235456', digest stable across calls.\n\nPROOF (compile-clean revert). Restoring only the one behavioural line\n  state[\"dirty_digest\"] = _fingerprint(status + \"\\n\" + _run(\"git\", \"diff\", \"HEAD\"))\nleaving _untracked_digest_lines() defined (ast.parse: 'compiles clean'), then\n  python3 -B -m unittest bench.memory.benchmarks.common.test_runmeta\nfails 2 of 65:\n\nFAIL: test_untracked_file_contents_reach_the_dirty_digest\n  AssertionError: 'sha256:fd371ee20fa0' == 'sha256:fd371ee20fa0' : two untracked implementations serialize to one provenance\n\nFAIL: test_untracked_content_hashing_is_budgeted\n  self.assertNotEqual(base[\"dirty_digest\"], resized[\"dirty_digest\"])\n  AssertionError: 'sha256:2cdf5f6d9c97' == 'sha256:2cdf5f6d9c97'\n\nWith the fix restored: Ran 65 tests, OK; and the full CI guard set (test_runmeta + ci.test_locomo_search_retry_patch) Ran 76 tests, OK, after merging origin/main (go build ./... clean).","to":"resolved"},"reviewId":"01M1P7ADFK2VD1J3H6Y5PQM0ND","targetId":"01M1P7ADG7SEZZ4HCA7FTVDN5Q","targetType":"review_comment","trailId":"01M1NC2KDB8G41TMVXFNRMSDX4"},"event":"comment.status_changed"}
